  "notes": [
    "No signer/RPC/client/ledger/runtime transport/HTTP/TLS dependency.",
    "Reused of1-range-recorder has zero enabled features; source/lock unchanged.",
    "Zstd uses bundled C with existing native compiler; no dynamic libzstd, CMake or protobuf compiler required.",
    "Manually declared prost projection pins official proto bytes; not a second Pump decoder.",
    "One local pump-protocol-v2 path dependency reuses exact B3 layout parsers. Borsh/derive and TOML proc-macro dependencies are locked, pure build-time/Rust support; no candidate-count override or network source added. Existing B3 source evidence matrices remain unchanged.",
    "Pinned solana-pubkey 4.3.0 with curve25519 enables local PDA derivation only. Twelve locked support packages add pure-Rust curve/SHA/compile-time arithmetic and macros; no RPC, signer or HTTP client. solana-define-syscall is target-conditional address/hash support, not a network client. SDK is source-inspected only, not a dependency.",
    "Local sell follow-up: borsh =1.8.0 is now also a direct dependency (defaults disabled, std enabled) solely to reuse the existing bounded TradeEvent BorshDeserialize implementation. Resolved packages, features, licenses and build scripts are byte-for-byte equal to the prior reviewed graph. No package download or new runtime capability."
  ]
